if you want to hang out and talk about  anime theories recommendations and other  fun stuff feel free to join us on  discord and twitch both links are in the  description what is up everybody its  Anna Mak here for anime uproar and in  this video we will be talking about  Durance true intentions and motivations  which have been finally revealed in  episode 130 of Dragon Ball super in  previous episodes we've gotten some  clues about Durin's past his philosophy  on life and the driving force behind his  commitment to become strong but an  episode 130 all the pretenses were  dropped and we finally saw who Jaron  really is and how far he is willing to  go in the name of his beliefs  the real jiren is very different from  what we were led to believe when he was  first introduced as a pride trooper and  a defender of justice there is a much  darker side to Jared and that is what we  will be talking about in this video if  you enjoyed the Dragon Ball super  content on this channel be sure to leave  a like to let me know if you're new to  the channel don't forget to subscribe  and hit that notification bell and we  post daily anime content on Twitter and  Instagram so come and check us out at  anime uproar in episode 130 as he is  losing the upper hand against the  mastered ultra instinct Goku in battle  jiren loses his cool he becomes almost  desperate and he repeats once again that  he cannot lose no matter what cheerin  believes that strength is justice  strength is absolute everything is  meaningless without victory to be  defeated is to lose everything now it  might sound like gern is just saying  random things here because he is so  shocked and angry that he can't seem to  defeat Goku but in reality jiren is  revealing to us his entire outlook on  life his philosophy about justice we  know that the pride troopers and  especially topo like to talk a lot about  this idea of Justice doing what's right  protecting the innocent defeating  evildoers and so on and while the exact  definition of justice is a complicated  question that  has been debated for thousands of years  when we talk about justice this is  usually what we think of protecting the  innocent punishing evildoers and  fighting for what's right but an episode  130 Geron reveals that he doesn't  actually believe in this idea of justice  at all Kieran's commitment to the Pride  troopers and to defending justice was a  lie  during his showdown with Goku Jaron has  a flashback to when he lost his parents  and comrades at the hands of the  mysterious evildoer from his past and  this traumatic memory and the desire to  never let something like this happen  again drives him to unlock his hidden  power cheerin vows that no matter what  he will never lose because losing to him  is the worst thing in the world as he  says to be defeated is to lose  everything  Durin's tragic past shaped his outlook  on life his philosophy and the view of  justice that he now holds the thing that  he really believes in is the concept of  might makes right and what does this  mean  basically this means that there is no  right and wrong at all  there is no such thing as justice those  who are strong and have power determine  what is right and what is wrong they  decide what justice is because they are  strong and others are weak they force  everyone else to accept their rules  about what is right and what is wrong  those who are strong create their own  definition of justice and this  definition is designed to benefit them  the strong define justice and what is  right and wrong in a way that suits them  and there is nothing that the weak can  do about it simply put it is the idea  that history is written by the victors  those who win decide what is true what  is right and what is just that is why  jiren says strength is justice if I am  strong and you are weak I get to decide  what is right and what is wrong and you  have to accept it if you don't I can  destroy you because I am stronger we can  definitely see how jiren came to believe  that might makes right he has a tragic  past where an evildoer destroyed his  family and kill  his friends when they tried to stand up  to him because he was strong and they  were weak the ideas of good and evil  right and wrong just and unjust did not  matter to the evildoer he was strong and  he did what he wanted his victims were  weaker and so they suffered jiren saw  this and he came to the conclusion that  justice doesn't matter the idea of  justice and right and wrong is not going  to stop a villain from hurting an  innocent person the only thing that will  stop him is strength and this is why  jiren believed that strength is the only  justice because strength is absolute you  can debate about the definition of  justice all you want but words cannot  protect you from fists the only thing  that can protect you is to get stronger  than your enemy the really interesting  thing about episode 130 is the fact that  in this episode jeera and Goku are not  only fighting physically their personal  philosophies are clashing as well  because of his belief that strength is  justice and that might makes right jiren  doesn't trust anyone but himself  he thinks that putting faith in others  is foolish because the only thing that  you can trust is your own strength on  the other hand as Crillon points out  from the stands Goku always springs back  no matter what  Krillin piccolo Vegeta Gohan Android 18  and all of the other members of universe  7 believe in Goku they place their faith  in Goku cheerin asks Goku how he keeps  getting up after getting beaten so many  times and Goku tells him that it is  because all of the people that he cares  about are trusting in him they believe  in him and depend on him and because of  the faith that they put in him he never  backs down the people that believe in  Goku give him strength to go on  Goku knows that the reason he is where  he is today the reason he became as  strong as he did is because he had the  support of all of his friends along the  way and this made him stronger some of  his friends started out as enemies and  they fought each other and trained each  other and became stronger together  jaren is furious when he hears this  because it is so different from his own  beliefs jiren asks who cares about  friendship  who cares about trusting in others to  accept that these things matter would be  to deny everything he'd ever been all of  his own beliefs jiren warns Goku that  the power you get from placing your  faith and others is easily erased and  then he does something that I really  didn't see coming  jiren shoots an energy blast not at Goku  but at the stands where Goku's friends  are watching the fight this energy blast  this act of aggression reveals Durance  true nature the real jiren and how far  he is willing to go to prove his point  goku manages to deflect the blast and  save his friends and we could argue that  even if goku didn't get there in time  the gods of destruction and angels would  have stopped it but we can't be 100%  sure so what jiren did was truly extreme  jiren put the lives of innocent people  at risk just to prove to goku that  strength is all that matters just to  prove that strength and power determine  who is right and who is wrong and things  like justice friendship and trust are  meaningless in the face of overwhelming  force if we think about this in terms of  international relations  Durin's view is actually pretty common  and even realistic if a stronger country  attacks a weaker country the weaker  country can talk about how the attack  violates international law how it is  morally wrong and unjust but if the  stronger country doesn't care about  those things then those things are  meaningless words and complaints will  not protect the weaker country from  their enemies tanks and fighter planes  so I can kind of see where jiren is  coming from but on the other hand the  story of Dragon Ball is the story of how  enemies can become friends and how  others can inspire us to train harder  and to fight against all odds to protect  the people we care about  Goku even says that he is not a hero of  justice or anything and of course the  Pride troopers used to talk a big game  about being heroes of justice but Goku  says that he will not forgive those who  try to hurt the people he cares about so  this truly is a clash of philosophies  the philosophy of might makes right and  the idea that your own strength is all  that matters  versus the philosophy that in life we  depend on others and that we need our  friends and the people we care about to  make us better and stronger people  personally I really enjoyed the fight  itself but I also enjoyed this  additional philosophical layer to the  showdown between Goku and jiren I have  to say that I was really surprised to  see Jaron try to attack go who's friends  in the stands that to me really revealed  the gerunds true nature beneath the calm  and quiet exterior there is a much  darker side to Jaron and he is willing  to do whatever it takes even Foote  innocent people in danger to prove his  point and justify his philosophy this  really does add an extra layer to  jaren's character he is not the hero of  Justice that he claimed to be in fact in  some ways he is the exact opposite of  that but let me know what you guys think  did your opinion of Jaron change after  episode 130 and what do you think about  the clash of philosophies do you agree  with jiren that might makes right and  that the only thing you can depend on is  your own strength or do you agree with  Goku that other people can make you  stronger and that you should depend on  your friends for support let me know  down in the comments if you enjoyed this  video I want to see more like it be sure  to leave a like to let me know if you  are new to the channel don't forget  subscribe and hit that notification bell  big THANK YOU to Cuusoo Murray for  sending me another one of his awesome  fan art of mastered ultra instinct Goku  I will link to his social media in the  description be sure to check him out and  show him some love if you want to have  your art featured in one of our future  videos be sure to follow us on Twitter  and Instagram at anime uproar as always  thank you all so much for watching and  until next time see us space cowboys  [Music]  you  [Music]

